.TH LIBMPQ__UPDATE_RENAME 3 2026-09-25 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__update_rename \- rename a named member in a staged MPQ update
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__update_rename(mpq_update_s *update, const char *old_filename, const char *new_filename);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Renames an existing member in the private working copy. The new name must not already exist. Encrypted members are decoded under the old name and re-encoded under the new name so filename-derived keys remain correct. The original archive remains unchanged until commit.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \fBLIBMPQ_SUCCESS\fP on success, or a negative libmpq error.
.SH ERRORS
A missing old name or existing new name returns LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST. Renaming an encrypted member whose physical block is shared by another name returns LIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT. Decryption, allocation, encoding, and I/O errors may also be returned.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq__update_remove (3),
.BR libmpq__update_commit (3)
